- Point 11 reading: capped-table-plus-disclosure-button satisfies "may be collapsed behind a
  disclosure" as written; flagging the reading for the record per instructions, not as a
  defect.
- Point 10: toggle-expanded state does not persist across an HTMX preset swap (resets to
  collapsed each time) — by design per RF.3.D, not a regression.
- Global focus-ring color/width (indigo, 3px) is inherited by RF3's new button, not
  introduced by RF3; noted only because it is the visible-focus evidence for point 9.
- `web/static/css/tailwind.css` is modified on disk (RF1's stone-token rebuild) but is not
